{"kind":"assert","text":"C1 (21f6d3cd) is built at 4fac2063 on builder/c1-custody-v2-20261113 (on main 8cbd3c61), with its tests passing. It waits for its gate slot after CF-1 and IE-1+FG-1. Two rules could not be held as written. Each needs a planner ruling before review.\n\n1. When a signing closes. Client note section 3 says a signing is closed when each of its copies has a refusal. Ruling 72b1d654's nine-submit test needs the eight signings refused `revision-moved` to stay open, or the ninth submit would sign. C1 closes a signing only on a `not-found` read after the signing dies, on `absent`, on `mismatch`, or when a fold names another intent. The latest signing of an unresolved record stays open, as in version 1. Proposal: section 3 adopts that list, and the note says that a refusal alone does not close a signing.\n\n2. `folded` widens two types. The ruled `folded` outcome adds a variant to `Sent` and to `Decided`. The MCP service, the hosted agent and packages/client/src/install-request.ts each gain a branch that treats a folded record as `unreadable`. None of them calls `folded`. Proposal: keep the branch, and state it in the C1 note.\n\nRecorded in the C1 note, with no ruling asked:\n- The note's `Signing` type is exported as `CustodySigning`, because intent.ts already exports `Signing`.\n- MCP `settle` on a refused record reads until that record's signing is dead and gets `not-found`. The answers keep their shape.\n- A write that only closes signings reports no metrics transition.\n- Only `memoryStore` changes, gaining `byTarget` and `observe`. The file, sqlite, durableCustody and durableRequestStore stores do not change. The store port reads and writes version 1 or version 2.\n- Three seals adopted: mcp/src/hosted.ts, mcp/src/hosted-retirement.ts and service.ts:McpService.\n- apps/views/test/two-process.test.mjs fails 3 cases on main 8cbd3c61 the same way it fails on C1. The gate's Node stage does not list that file. Request 8fd9ffe0 covers it."}